The phase obtained from the sensor was converted into the Optical Path Difference (OPD) corresponding to free-space propagation in vacuum, using the relation $OPD = \Phi\lambda/{2\pi}$, where $\Phi$ is the phase and $\lambda$ is the wavelength. Phase measurements were conducted at varying target intensities, creating distinct regimes of laser-matter interaction. At each intensity level, 10 laser shots were taken, and the phases were averaged to reduce numerical error.   

