Assume that $(X,\met,\m)$ is an essentially nonbranching metric measure space satisfying $\CD(\eta (N-1), N)$ for $N>1$, and $f: I \rightarrow [0, \infty)$ is smooth with $f''- \kappa f\leq 0$, $-(f')^2 + \kappa f^2 \leq \eta$. Then the generalized cone ${}^-\!I\times_f X$ equipped with the measure $f(t)^N \,\dint t \otimes\dint\m$, satisfies $\tmcp(-\kappa N, N+1)$. 
\end{ithm}
\setcounter{subsection}{5}
\setcounter{ithm}{5}
By verbatim the same proof we get the corresponding result for $I\times_f^N X$.
\begin{ithm}[From $X$ to ${}^+I\times^N_fX$] Assume that $(X,\met,\m)$ is an essentially nonbranching metric measure space satisfying $\CD(\eta (N-1), N)$ for $N>1$. Assume $f:I\rightarrow[0,\infty)$ is smooth and satisfies
 $f''+ \kappa f\leq 0$ and  $(f')^2 + \kappa f^2 \leq \eta$. 
Then $I\times_f^N X$, i.e., the generalized cone $I\times_f X$ equipped with the measure $f(t)^N \,\dint t \otimes\dint\m$, satisfies $\mcp(\kappa N, N+1)$. 
