\subsection{Breather solution in the modified Noguchi electrical transmission line}
To construct a breather solution of the considered electrical transmission line, we consider
\begin{equation}
V_{nb}(t)=\epsilon\psi_b(\zeta,\tau)e^{i\theta}+\epsilon^2\psi_{10}(\zeta,\tau)+\epsilon^2 \psi_{20}(\zeta,\tau)e^{2i\theta}+c.c.,
\label{eqb3}
\end{equation}
where $\psi(\zeta,\tau)$, $\psi_{10}(\zeta,\tau)$ and $\psi_{20}(\zeta,\tau)$ are given in Eqs. (\ref{eqb2}), (\ref{eq8}) and (\ref{eq81}). Equation (\ref{eqb3}) describes the dynamics of breathers in the electrical transmission line.

