We include commonly used synthetic datasets for benchmarking purposes during clustering. These are \texttt{Blobs}, \texttt{Circles}, and \texttt{Moons}, all imported through \texttt{scikit-learn} \cite{pedregosa2011scikit}. Each sample has two features, the x- and y-coordinate, and we take the number of clusters to represent different classes for the classification part. We manually assign a label to each cluster. \texttt{Blobs} will have three classes, and \texttt{Moons} and \texttt{Circles} will only have two. The \texttt{Blobs}, \texttt{Moons}, and \texttt{Circles} datasets were generated with the following parameters, respectively: a cluster standard deviation of 1.40 for \texttt{Blobs}, noise of 0.075 for \texttt{Moons}, and noise of 0.1 with a factor of 0.2 for \texttt{Circles}.


