A \ac{pdfa} $\pdfa$ is \emph{canonical} if for any $\pdfa'$ equivalent to $\pdfa$, the number of states in $\pdfa$ is no greater than the number of states in $\pdfa'$.

        A \ac{pnfa} $\pdfa= \langle Q, \Sigma, \delta, q_0, O, \succeq, \lambda \rangle$ generalizes a \ac{pdfa} by allowing its transition function to be nondeterministic, i.e., $\delta: Q \times \Sigma \rightarrow 2^Q$, and its ranking function to be incomplete.
        %
        When the ranking of a state $q$  is undefined, it is denoted $\lambda(q) =  \undefined$.

