        Theorem~\ref{thr:NP-Complete} shows that our automata inference problem, the \MCPDFA problem, is generally hard. 
        In the next section, we present an efficient algorithm that  learns the canonical presentation of the true \ac{pdfa} from which the sample is generated, provided the sample satisfies certain conditions. % That kind of sample is a specific type of inputs for which \MCPDFA can be solved efficiently.
