\begin{definition}
Given a partition $\pi$ of $Q$, and two blocks $B_i, B_j \in \pi$,  the \emph{join} of $B_i$ and $B_j$, denoted $J(\pi, B_i, B_j)$, is the partition obtained from $\pi$ by combining $B_i$ and $B_j$, i.e.,
        \begin{multline*}
            J(\pi, B_i, B_j) =  \left( \pi\setminus \{B_i, B_j\} \right) \cup 
                \{B_i \cup B_j\}. \notag
        \end{multline*}
\end{definition}
        This `join' operation is also called \emph{merging} in the context of automata learning.

