 Accordingly, we define a new operation $DJ$, called the \emph{deterministic join}, which produces a quotient automaton:
 $$
 \pnfa_0 / DJ(\pi, B_i, B_j) = D(\pnfa_0 / J(\pi, B_i, B_j)).
