Finally,  the \ac{pdfa} learning algorithm is described in Alg.~\ref{alg:euclid}. It uses a function $\eta: 2^{W_S} \setminus \emptyset \rightarrow \Sigma^*$, referred to as  the \emph{block-name} function, such that for each $U \in 2^{W_S} \setminus \emptyset$,
$\eta(U)$ is the smallest word within $U$ given the lexicographical ordering, i.e., $\eta(U)=\min_{<_L}\{w \in U\}$.
%
%\deleted{Given a partition $\pi$ and a word $w \in W$, we abuse the notation and use $\eta^{-1}(w, \pi)$ to denote the block $B \in \pi$ such that $\eta(B) = w$.
