\section{Introduction}
%Controlling partial differential equation (PDE) systems remains a highly challenging task due to the infinite-dimensional nature of the state space and the complexity of system dynamics. Learning-based approaches integrated with the classical control theory have emerged as a promising alternative, offering data-driven adaptability. However, one of the key challenges in combining classical control theory with learning-based methods lies in effectively incorporating prior knowledge from classical control into neural network learning.

