         ibaf-graph) dragging vibrates the
         graph. This is a consequence of the ``elastic'' option (the
         default) which continually redraws nodes/links for graphical
         animation, but animation/vibration can be suppressed by
         toggling to ``snap'' --- enter ``{\bf d}'' to toggle between
         the two --- in the drag-reminder ``{\bf elstc/snap-d}'' or
         ``{\bf snap/elstc-d}'' indicates which drag method is
         active. With ``snap'' just the active node is dragged leaving
         a trail as in figure~ \ref{snap/elastic}.  On release the node (+fragment)
          and links ``{\bf snap}'' into place and the trail
          disappears. For large graphs ``{\bf snap}'' is a more efficient method.

