\subsection{Order parameter probability distribution}\label{ssec:orderparameterprobabdist}

Let us consider a first-order phase transition with two distinct phases. By definition, at the critical point the two phases have equal probabilities in the large-volume limit.  A schematic order parameter distribution is shown in Fig.~\ref{fig:schematic}: the two high probability peaks in the distribution correspond to the order parameter values characteristic for the two distinct bulk phases, which are bridged by a mixed phase region with suppressed probability.  

