\subsection{Plaquette discontinuity}\label{ssec:plaquettediscontinuity}

We measure the plaquette discontinuity by separate simulations at $\beta_c$, prepared so that the system is fully in the confined or the deconfined phase, and using large enough volumes so that the system remains in the same phase throughout the simulation. The measured plaquette values for confined and deconfined phases are listed in the 5th resp. 6th comlumn of Table~\ref{tab:latentheatcompdat}. Due to the large volumes, the confined phase simulations suffer from topological freezing. Since the Euclidean gauge action grows with the absolute value of the topological charge (cf. Fig.~\ref{fig:plaqvstopo}), we incorporated a systematic uncertainty of order $2\times 10^{-6}$ in the error of the plaquette difference in the second to last column of Table~\ref{tab:latentheatcompdat} of Appendix~\ref{app:lhtables}. 

