The continuum extrapolated values ($\sim\,N_t=\infty$) for the latent heat are obtained analogously to those for the interface tension, i.e., by fitting for each $\SU{N}$ the linear function \eqref{eq:itcontinuumfit} to the data sets $\sscof{\ssof{1/N_t^2,L/\ssof{N^2\,T_c^4}}\vert N_t>5}$ where we again exclude $N_t=5$. The fits are shown in the upper panel of Fig.~\ref{fig:latentheatfits} and the fit results are listed in Table~\ref{tab:latheatcontinuumlim} of Appendix~\ref{app:lhtables}.  

