The paper is organized as follows. Section \ref{sec:obs}  describes the {\it JWST}/NIRCam observations and the photometry. The source-plane size constraints are presented in Section \ref{sec:size}. Section~\ref{sec:posydon} examines which simulated binary systems are within the observational constraints and analyzes the evolutionary histories of the most likely systems. In Section \ref{sec:orbit}, we model how the magnifications of each star in a binary configuration vary with time as the stars orbit one another across the microlensing caustic. Section \ref{sec:conclusion}  discusses the results and summarizes our conclusions. 
