    \textbf{Magnus expansion analysis of the $\mathcal{PT}$ phase transition and band structures.} (a) Open circles, dashed lines, and solid lines are direct numerical ODE solutions, zeroth-order, and second-order Magnus analysis results, respectively. Fixed parameters: $\epsilon_{\mathrm{i}}=1.8$, $k_0 = \omega_\text{m} / (2\mathrm{\pi} c)$. The horizontal green line indicates $\mathrm{Tr}(U)/2 = -1$. (b-d) Blue solid lines show the real parts of the $\Omega(k_z)T$, while red dashed lines represent the imaginary parts, for three different values of $\gamma=\{0.9, 1.0, 1.1\}$. 
}
