\end{equation}
where $\| \cdot \|_{\ell^2}$ denotes the standard $\ell^2$-norm of the vector of degrees of freedom.

In all cases, we observe that the number of iterations decreases as $\epsilon$ decreases, in agreement with \cref{Thm:aug}.
Moreover, the number of iterations remains uniformly bounded as the mesh is refined.
Hence, we conclude that \cref{Alg:aug} converges in very few iterations even for small values of $h$, provided that $\epsilon$ is sufficiently small.
These results support our claim that the mixed problem~\eqref{mixed_FEM_saddle} can be reduced to the optimization problem~\eqref{mixed_FEM_nearly}.

