\subsubsection{Quantum circuits}

The quantum circuits implementing Algorithm~\ref{proposed_algorithm} for edge detection on a $64 \times 64$ grayscale image are shown in Figure~\ref{fig:quantum_circuits}. In this example, a total of $n = 6 + 6 = 12$ qubits are used to represent the flattened image, along with one additional ancilla qubit required for the high-pass filtering operation within Algorithm~\ref{proposed_algorithm}. 

Each circuit consists of three main stages: the sequency-ordered Walsh–Hadamard transform (WHT), the high-pass filtering stage, and the inverse WHT. The segment before the second barrier corresponds to the WHT, while the segment after the third barrier implements its inverse. The high-pass filtering operation, which corresponds to Step~4 of Algorithm~\ref{proposed_algorithm}, is applied between the second and third barriers.

